notes               = "Untitled in source. Two lines. مربع خنده‌ها, the square of her laughter, is one of the poet's fixed images — it appears inside adobe-birdsong (page 72) and the Alizadeh letter (79–82), and as چهارگوش خنده‌ها in gray-gaze (88); here it gets a whole poem to itself. ۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۶ is 6 Dey, which falls on 27 December 1989 — a day-level date, so the Gregorian is resolved exactly rather than by the +622 winter rounding. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

اگر مربع خنده‌های تو نباشد
آرزوهایم را کُجا نقاشی کنم...
۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۶

===machine===

If the square of your laughter were not there
where would I paint my longings...
1368/10/6

===lantern===

If the square of your laughter were not there,
where would I paint what I long for...

1368/10/6

===translation===

===footnotes===

Everywhere else in the book the square of her laughter is a place inside a longer
poem — something else happens in it. Here the whole poem is the question of what he would do
without it, and the answer is that he would have nowhere to put the painting.

